Z||000004||Shaun41178||04-14-99||06:33 PM||||Pretender, yes my engine is completly stock.  It does have a standard rebuild about 29k miles ago and as far as I know it uses all stock parts, nothing special.  only mod is the ignition and then I have ported the exhaust manifolds just recently.  I have been using it for almost a year without engine problems.  Nothing has blown up.  I don't plan on having it blow up either.  nitrous is a good power adder if used wisely.  50 hp is not a lot and any stock 2.8 v6 should/would have no problem handling it unless there is already major engien problems or excessive blowby.  Even after using it for almost a year, my engine oil still comes out almost as clean as it went in.  So I think my rings are still sealing real good.  No blowby or very very little
